    "input_texts": [
      "Title: ServiceNow Filter UI: Field Choosers and Value Selection\nDescription: Key UI patterns and pitfalls observed when constructing complex AND filters.\n- The initial field chooser uses a combobox with the text 'All of these conditions must be met. -- choose field --'.\n- Once a field is selected, the value is set via a secondary combobox labeled 'Choose option for field: [FieldName]' or a direct textbox for string inputs.\n- Direct clicking on dropdown options (e.g., clicking 'Normal') may fail; using the `select_option` action on the combobox is more reliable.\n- The 'Model' field supports an 'is empty string' operator, which must be selected from the operator combobox (e.g., 'Operator For Condition 3: Model is').\n- After setting a condition, a specific button appears to add the next AND condition, labeled 'Add AND Condition To Condition X: [Previous Field] is [Value]'.\n- The filter logic is strictly AND ('All of these conditions must be met') within the active group until a new OR group is initiated.\n- Field choosers for new conditions are automatically focused when the 'Add AND Condition' button is clicked.\n- The trajectory indicates the workflow can proceed sequentially without needing to re-open the field chooser for the next step."
    ],
